All strategies incur capability cost relative to the base model; binary filtering partially mitigates this for reasoning tasks.
Cross-model replication and rate sweeps (10--100\%) confirm graduated $\approx$ no-filter ordering (Appendix~\ref{sec:pythia_filtering}, \ref{sec:dose_response}, \ref{sec:rate_sweep}).

